.TH XNVME-PERF-XFER-REGISTER 1 "22 November 2026" "xNVMe" "xNVMe"
.SH NAME
\fBxnvme-perf-xfer-register \fP- Register the dma-buf the process inherited as \fB--dmabuf-fd\fP with the device
\fB-\fB-count\fP times, unregistering it after each, and report the microseconds
\fBeach call took. The dma-buf is named by addresses reserved with PROT_NONE,
\fBwhich nothing reads or writes; its size is the exporter's. With \fB--homi-id\fP
\fBthe registrations go through the server.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.fam C
\fBxnvme-perf-xfer\fP \fIregister\fP <uri> [<args>]
.fam T
.fi
.fam T
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Register the dma-buf the process inherited as \fB--dmabuf-fd\fP with the device
\fB--count\fP times, unregistering it after each, and report the microseconds
each call took. The dma-buf is named by addresses reserved with PROT_NONE,
which nothing reads or writes; its size is the exporter's. With \fB--homi-id\fP
the registrations go through the server.
.SH REQUIRED
.TP
.B
<uri>
Device URI e.g. '/dev/nvme0n1', '0000:01:00.1', '10.9.8.1:8888', '\\.\PhysicalDrive1'
.TP
.B
\fB--dmabuf-fd\fP NUM
A dma-buf the process inherited as this fd, for the payloads
.RE
.PP

.SH OPTIONAL
